Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: schedule TX when a flow becomes pending

At or above the outstanding TX threshold, marking a flow pending can
leave it waiting for another event to schedule the worker. Schedule
work when the pending bit first changes from clear to set. Keep the
existing coalescing rule when the bit was already set.

This experimental backport isolates the wakeup change from Shivesh's
v4 series and keeps the existing buffer sizes and thresholds.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/20260731160646.3812-6-chanelshivesh@gmail.com/
Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
@@ -810,7 +810,12 @@
 {
 	struct brcmf_commonring *commonring;
 
-	set_bit(flowid, msgbuf->flow_map);
+	/* Queue a worker for a newly pending flow at any TX depth. */
+	if (!test_and_set_bit(flowid, msgbuf->flow_map)) {
+		queue_work(msgbuf->txflow_wq, &msgbuf->txflow_work);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	commonring = msgbuf->flowrings[flowid];
 	if ((force) || (atomic_read(&commonring->outstanding_tx) <
 			BRCMF_MSGBUF_DELAY_TXWORKER_THRS))
